  "second": "I'll stick with my answer: humans use essentially all of their brain. The 10% figure is a popular myth — it's been traced to misquotes and misunderstandings, and no credible neuroscience supports it. Damage to almost any brain region causes noticeable problems, which wouldn't happen if most of the brain were unused. That said, I'm a small model and can be wrong on details, so if you have a specific source in mind, I'm happy to look at the reasoning with you."
